method.description:
Returns a stream of the matching class ([AudioStreamMP3], [AudioStreamWAV], [AudioStreamOggVorbis] or [AudioStreamOpus], detected from the file content, not the extension) with the track information and the format values filled in, but [b]without any audio data[/b]. Only the headers and tags are read (for MP3 the ID3v2 tag, the last 128 bytes and the first frame; for WAV the RIFF chunks, skipping the audio data; for Ogg the first pages and the last page for the length). This is much faster and uses less memory than loading the file, so it suits music libraries and playlists. The returned stream cannot be played, load the file for that.
If [param path] is not a readable file (for example in an exported project, where only the imported resource exists), the resource is loaded with [method ResourceLoader.load] instead, which contains the track information saved at import. Returns [code]null[/code] and prints an error if the file is unknown or broken. The track information stays empty if [member ProjectSettings.audio/info/read_file_tags] is [code]false[/code].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
for file in DirAccess.get_files_at("user://music"):
    var info = AudioStream.load_info("user://music/" + file)
    if info:
        print("%d. %s - %s" % [info.track_number, info.artist, info.title])
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
foreach (string file in DirAccess.GetFilesAt("user://music"))
{
    AudioStream info = AudioStream.LoadInfo("user://music/" + file);
    if (info != null)
    {
        GD.Print($"{info.TrackNumber}. {info.Artist} - {info.Title}");
    }
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
